--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Monday, the 5th of January, 1931 (1/3 key facts kept) ---
I pawned my wedding ring to raise 5s. Od. for Mrs. Win Riley, who went away without repaying me. I read in the evening paper of the death of the Princess Royal, and saw that she had been ill for some months, but that this was the first recent indication of recurrence of heart trouble. I also read that Millwall had beaten Charlton by six goals to nil in football.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Monday, the 5th of January, 1931 (0/0 key facts kept) ---
I read in the Daily Herald the news of the death of Princess Louise, the King's eldest sister, and I felt sorry. I also read the news of the defeat of Charlton by Millwall, and I felt glad.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Monday, the 5th of January, 1931 (0/0 key facts kept) ---
I read in The Times the death of the Princess Royal, and the increased weakness of Princess Louise.
